<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tribal Hidage</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tribal Hidage is an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-saxons">Anglo-Saxon</a> list of 35 peoples south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humber">Humber</a>, giving the number of hides, units of land assessment, attributed to each. It probably records tribute owed to a Mercian or possibly Northumbrian overlord and is usually dated between the 7th and 9th centuries; the oldest copy is an 11th-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a>. Many of the small groups it names, such as the Elmetsæte, are otherwise almost unknown.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tribal-hidage.jpg" alt="Tribal Hidage" width="320" height="348" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Topographic_Map_of_the_UK_-_Blank.png: Equestenebrarum derivative work: Amitchell125 at English Wikipedia · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tribal_Hidage_2.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
